<!--
  suspendWrappedResponseAfterForward="false"

  Tomcat 11 defaults this Context attribute to true (Tomcat 9 and 10.1 default to false). With it
  true, once a RequestDispatcher.forward() returns through a wrapped response, Tomcat unwraps to its
  own ResponseFacade and SUSPENDS it instead of calling close() on the outer wrapper (Tomcat bug 68634,
  added for session-replication ordering in clusters). Any filter wrapper that still holds buffered
  output at that point then flushes into a suspended response, and Tomcat silently discards the bytes.

  JavaMelody's MonitoringFilter is such a wrapper (an 8 KiB OutputStreamWriter drained after the
  chain returns; javamelody/javamelody#1306). XNAT serves every /pages/view/** admin page by a Spring
  MVC forward to a JSP, so on Tomcat 11 those pages arrived truncated at the last 8 KiB boundary and
  pages under 8 KiB arrived empty, with HTTP 200 and nothing logged. Manage Users and Site
  Administration rendered as a blank body with a spinner.

  Setting the attribute to false restores the pre-11 behavior: the outer wrapper is closed, which
  flushes it.  In a clustered deployment with session replication, the reply can reach the client before
  the session has been replicated, and a follow-up request routed to another node may not find it.
  It only matters if you run Tomcat clustering with replicated sessions and a load balancer without sticky sessions.
  When not running with clustered session replication, the ordering the true setting was
  introduced for does not apply. Advice is to use session pinning rather than rely on this ordering anyway.

  Remove this once XNAT ships a JavaMelody release containing the
  #1306 fix (not in 2.8.0).

  The attribute exists from Tomcat 9.0.87 / 10.1.20 onward, where false is already the default. An
  older Tomcat logs a "did not find a matching property" warning at startup and ignores it.
-->
<Context suspendWrappedResponseAfterForward="false">
    <!--
    For Tomcat 7 compatibility, uncomment the <Loader> element and comment out the <Resources>
    and <CookieProcessor> elements under that.
    -->
    <!-- Loader className="org.apache.catalina.loader.VirtualWebappLoader" searchVirtualFirst="true" virtualClasspath="${xnat.home}/plugins/*.jar"/ -->

    <!--
    For Tomcat 8 compatibility, uncomment the <Resources> and <CookieProcessor> elements below and
    comment out the <Loader> element below that.
    -->
    <Resources>
        <PreResources className="org.apache.catalina.webresources.DirResourceSet" base="${xnat.home}/plugins" webAppMount="/WEB-INF/lib" />
    </Resources>
   <!-- <CookieProcessor className="org.apache.tomcat.util.http.LegacyCookieProcessor" /> -->y
    <JarScanner scanAllDirectories="true" />
    <Parameter name="xnatHome" value="${xnat.home}"/>
    <Manager pathname="" />
</Context>
